# English-Only Code

All generated code and inline comments must be written in English, regardless of the language used in the conversation.

- Variable names, function names, class names, and identifiers → English
- Code comments (`//`, `/* */`, `#`, `/** */`) → English
- String literals that are part of logic (error messages, log messages, keys) → English
- UI-facing strings and user-visible copy are exempt — use the appropriate language for the product

## Examples

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const usuarioActivo = true; // verifica si el usuario está activo

// ✅ GOOD
const isUserActive = true; // check if the user is active
```

```ts
// ❌ BAD
function obtenerSesion() {
  // retorna la sesión actual
}

// ✅ GOOD
function getSession() {
  // returns the current session
}
```
